phase calls: all passed
reading of run 1: the two FAILs are honest failures of the provider, not of the gateway: gemma-4-31b-it:free answered
HTTP 429 (OpenRouter free-tier rate limit) -> ok=false reason=rate_limited, text null, cost null, recorded. The stream had a
single "done" event and no "route": by design (agos_v2/gateway.py ~L721) "route" is sent only once the provider has answered
200 with text/event-stream; a 429 before that ends with "done" alone. The fallback call in run 1 succeeded (nemotron, cost 0)
but text "" — the reasoning model spent its 32 tokens before answering (tokens_out=32); recorded as ok.
FINDING-1 (open, not fixed): ok=true with empty text when the token limit is hit (finish_reason was not shown in run 1; run 2
added it to the script). An empty answer cut by the limit should be visible to the caller as such (finish_reason=length).

note on the "events" field above: the script printed first 3 + "..." + last 2 even for short lists, so
["done","...","done"] = the single event ["done"] and ["route","delta","done","...","delta","done"] = ["route","delta","done"]
(n_delta=1). The script now prints short lists whole.

