## H. What this proves and what it does not
PROVEN live: real provider calls through the production gateway (1 provider: OpenRouter, free models, platform key under the
"free" policy), plain AND streamed (SSE through Render: 200 text/event-stream, route -> delta -> done, recorded), fallback across
routes with fallback_used and attempts, honest failures (rate_limited 429 from the provider, platform_key_not_allowed for a priced
model before any provider call, no_key, unknown model refused), call records written on production without prompt/answer.
NOT proven: three providers (only 1 so far — needs ≥2 more provider keys from the owner via the UI); cost match against the
provider's bill (cost_usd=0 is what OpenRouter reported in usage; matching the gen-… ids against the OpenRouter activity page needs
the platform key's account — owner); multi-delta streaming (the short answer came in 1 delta; a longer answer was not tried);
tools on a real provider; Anthropic streaming live. The unknown model is refused as platform_key_not_allowed (not in the catalog
= not provably free) — honest, but the reason name does not say "unknown model" (FINDING-3, open).
R-206 stays in_progress.

